<article class="env-definition" id="6D0F2A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/6D0F2A">Definition <span data-tag="6D0F2A">5.5.8.1</span> <span class="named">(<span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/homotopyvarieties">homotopyvarieties</a>]</span>)</span>.</a>siftedsimplicial set!sifted A simplicial set $K$ is <em>sifted</em> if it satisfies the following conditions: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The simplicial set $K$ is nonempty. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
The diagonal map $K \rightarrow K \times K$ is cofinal. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
